    "path_relative_to_mod": "docs/assets/gfx_fix_other_icons_resume/prompts/013_meteor_storm_command.md",
    "text": "Use case: stylized-concept\nAsset type: Hearts of Iron IV decision-category icon, processed to a 53x40 RGBA canvas with genuine transparency.\nPrimary request: Create an original, readable Meteor Storm Command icon for a national emergency category.\nInput image: The existing nd_cat_skyfall_emergency_bureau.png decode is a style-only anchor for aged bronze material and painted 3D relief. Transfer its warm antique-bronze finish and compact weight; do not copy its shape or subject.\nScene/backdrop: No scene backdrop. The unused canvas must be genuinely transparent.\nSubject: A small observatory dome with a telescope beneath a descending meteor and short fragment trail, all integrated as one bronze relief badge. Make the observatory and meteor legible at 53x40; do not include a person.\nStyle: Muted bronze and gold with dark recessed edges, restrained highlights, softly painted dimensional metal. Use a compact thin bronze bezel consistent with the reference family, without a square plaque or oversized ring.\nComposition/framing: Wide 4:3 icon composition, centered, with complete silhouette and margin on every side. Keep the main painted form within about 88% of the eventual canvas; plan for a clear 3 px margin after processing.\nLighting/mood: Restrained warm metal highlights, emergency but orderly.\nMaterials/textures: Aged bronze observatory dome and telescope, meteor with a warm molten core and a short, controlled trail.\nConstraints: One static icon; designed for native-size readability; use the exposed built-in ImageGen path.\nAvoid: Text, letters, numerals, flags, people, extra objects, UI elements, white outlines, sticker borders, broad glow, blur, fake checkerboard, opaque or chroma background, clipped edges, transparent holes in the painted subject, and a duplicate of the input image.",
